{"id":"a1f89420-c540-44d8-b5ae-eca961b7373e","object":"chat.completion","created":1795243720,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"SELECT level_id,\n       COUNT(*) AS member_count,\n       ROUND(SUM(valid_orders)::numeric / NULLIF(COUNT(*), 0), 2) AS avg_valid_orders_per_member,\n       ROUND(AVG(member_gmv), 2) AS avg_member_gmv\nFROM (\n    SELECT m.member_id,\n           m.level_id,\n           COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS valid_orders,\n           SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) AS member_gmv\n    FROM members m\n    LEFT JOIN customers c ON c.customer_unique_id = m.customer_unique_id\n    LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id\n                      AND o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled', 'unavailable')\n    LEFT JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n    GROUP BY m.member_id, m.level_id\n) t\nGROUP BY level_id\nORDER BY level_id NULLS LAST\nLIMIT 1000;","reasoning_content":"我们需要回答SQL。需要解析问题。需要按会员等级ID统计全部会员数（含无有效订单）、人均有效订单数；同时统计会员已知含运费GMV的平均值，无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值，不把未知金额当0。\n\n需要输出一条SELECT。需要确定表与连接。会员等级ID = members.level_id。全部会员数含无有效订单：以 members 为左起点，按 level_id 分组，COUNT(*) 或 COUNT(member_id)。人均有效订单数：每个会员等级的有效订单数 / 会员数？ 需要定义人均有效订单数 = 有效订单数 / 全部会员数（含无有效订单）。有效订单口径排除 canceled/unavailable。订单事实通过 orders.customer_id -> customers.customer_unique_id? members.customer_unique_id 关联。需要看 schema：members.member_id, customer_unique_id, level_id, status, points. customers.customer_id, customer_unique_id. orders.customer_id. 要将会员与订单关联：members.customer_unique_id = customers.customer_unique_id，然后 customers.customer_id = orders.customer_id。参考示例这样连接。订单可能多个订单项。有效订单数应按订单去重，用 COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id)。但含无有效订单的会员数：COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id)。人均有效订单数 = COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) / COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id)，但连接会：一个会员多个订单，会员数去重没问题；有效订单数去重。需要保留全部会员，LEFT JOIN customers ON unique, LEFT JOIN orders ON customer_id 并附加有效订单过滤需要放ON? 因为要全部会员。如果 WHERE o.order_status NOT IN ... 会删除无订单会员。需要把有效订单条件放在 LEFT JOIN orders 的 ON 子句中，或者用子查询预聚合有效订单。同时 GMV 平均：已知含运费GMV的平均值。这句话可能有歧义：按会员等级，会员的已知含运费GMV的平均值？ 即每个会员等级内，会员的GMV平均值（每个会员的GMV，无商品金额事实为NULL不参与均值，不把未知金额当0）。需要统计会员已知含运费GMV的平均值。可能 \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" = 对每个会员等级，计算每个会员的含运费GMV（订单项金额+运费），然后对这些会员的GMV取平均，仅包括有已知商品金额事实的会员，无商品金额事实为NULL不参与。不把未知金额当0。需要小心：GMV 是 SUM(oi.price+oi.freight_value) per member，然后 AVG over members。过滤订单有效口径（order_status NOT canceled/unavailable）默认。GMV metric with freight，过滤默认。需要按会员等级ID，包含全部会员数，人均有效订单数。GMV均值只包括有商品金额事实的会员。如果会员无订单/无金额事实，不应参与 AVG；但如果会员有订单但金额未知？ price numeric possibly NULL? 数据中 price 可能 NULL? 题目说无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值，不把未知金额当0。表达式 SUM(price+freight_value) 若 price NULL 且 freight非NULL，则求和忽略NULL? SUM(price+freight_value) 对行中任一 NULL 导致该行表达式 NULL，SUM 忽略。如果所有行都 NULL 或没有行，SUM 返回 NULL。AVG(SUM(...)) 会忽略 NULL。这符合无事实不参与。但需确保每个会员的 GMV 是 NULL 若没有有效订单项？ 若用 LEFT JOIN order_items 和 SUM(oi.price+oi.freight_value)，无订单项会员的 SUM 为 NULL。AVG 忽略。但若会员有订单但所有 oi.price+freight 为 NULL，SUM 为 NULL 忽略。Good.\n\n需要计算每个会员等级：会员数（全部会员，包括状态? 会员状态 status 1正常2冻结3注销。问题说全部会员数（含无有效订单），未指定排除注销等。不能擅自过滤状态。所以所有 members。按 level_id。人均有效订单数 = 有效订单总数 / 会员总数。有效订单需要关联订单，按订单主键去重。但若直接 LEFT JOIN orders 和 order_items，订单总数需 COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) per level。会员数 COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id)。GMV per member: 由于多个 order_items 和 orders，需先按会员聚合 GMV，再按等级取 AVG。如果在同一查询中直接按 level 分组并对 oi.price+freight 求和然后 AVG？ 不能得到会员平均，因为 AVG(每行金额) 不是会员平均。需要子查询按会员计算 GMV，然后外层按 level 求 AVG。但人均有效订单数和会员数也可在此子查询或单独聚合。\n\n可能构建：\nWITH member_orders AS (\n  SELECT m.member_id, m.level_id,\n         COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS valid_orders,\n         SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) AS member_gmv\n  FROM members m\n  LEFT JOIN customers c ON c.customer_unique_id = m.customer_unique_id\n  LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id AND o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\n  LEFT JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  GROUP BY m.member_id, m.level_id\n)\nSELECT level_id,\n       COUNT(*) AS member_count,\n       ROUND(SUM(valid_orders)::numeric / NULLIF(COUNT(*),0), 2) AS avg_valid_orders_per_member,\n       ROUND(AVG(member_gmv), 2) AS avg_member_gmv\nFROM member_orders\nGROUP BY level_id\nORDER BY level_id;\n\nBut potential issue: LEFT JOIN orders condition filters valid orders. Then LEFT JOIN order_items on o. For canceled orders, o.order_id NULL, order_items none. Good. But order_items join includes all order_items for valid orders. member_gmv = SUM(price+freight) per member. For members with no valid order, member_gmv NULL. AVG ignores NULL. Good. 会员数 COUNT(*) includes all members. 人均有效订单数: SUM(valid_orders)/COUNT(*) = total valid orders / all members. valid_orders counts distinct orders per member. If a member has multiple customers? member.customer_unique_id to customers.customer_unique_id may map multiple customer_ids. Fine. Could there be duplicate customers per unique? customer_unique_id not primary. There may be multiple customer_id rows same unique id. Joining can duplicate orders? Actually orders.customer_id unique per order? Each order has one customer_id. If member maps to multiple customer records (same unique), orders by those customer_ids may be multiple; COUNT DISTINCT order_id handles. GMV sum over order_items could duplicate if multiple customer rows match same order? No order_id has one customer_id, and each customer_id row maps to unique. If customers has duplicate rows with same customer_id? customer_id primary, no. If member.customer_unique_id equals multiple customer rows with different customer_id, each order belongs to one customer_id; no duplication of same order. Good. But if members have duplicate member rows same customer_unique_id? member_id primary; could multiple members same unique? Possibly? Then grouping by member_id, and level. Need all members. If multiple member records same unique and same level, orders repeated for each member in their member_gmv; that's per member. Fine.\n\nNeed consider \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" maybe they want AVG(SUM(oi.price+freight)) across all members? We do that. Unit: monetary ROUND 2. 人均有效订单数 maybe ROUND 2? It says 人均; no explicit decimals. Default for ratios? Rule 12: 未注册比例默认小数四位，明确百分比乘100两位。 This is not registered ratio? \"人均有效订单数\" is count per member, not exactly ratio? Could be average orders per member, likely ROUND 2? General amount/price/average ROUND two. It says 其余金额/单价/均值 ROUND 两位. 人均有效订单数 is 均值, so ROUND 2. Good. GMV average ROUND 2.\n\nNeed output columns: level_id, 会员数, 人均有效订单数, GMV均值. Chinese aliases? SQL can use aliases. We can use AS member_count, avg_valid_orders, avg_gmv. No need names. Use member_levels? No, only level_id. Could join member_levels to ensure levels? The question asks by member level ID, all members. If some level_id in members not in member_levels? Should we include? \"按会员等级ID统计全部会员数\" from members. No need member_levels. If want only defined levels? Not specified. Use members.\n\nNeed ensure \"全部会员数（含无有效订单）\" includes members with no orders. Our member_orders starts from members and left joins. But then GROUP BY member_id, level_id. COUNT(*) outer per level counts all members. Good. However there is a subtlety: In member_orders, LEFT JOIN customers may fail if no matching customer; then no orders; member_gmv NULL, valid_orders 0. Good.\n\nNeed \"无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值\" If member has valid orders but order_items row with price+freight non-null. If price NULL but freight non-null, expression NULL; sum ignores that item. If all items null, member_gmv NULL. AVG ignores. But if member has zero order_items, member_gmv NULL. Good.\n\nNeed \"不把未知金额当0\": not COALESCE member_gmv. Good.\n\nPotential issue GMV expression uses oi.price + oi.freight_value; if freight_value NULL and price non-null, expression NULL, entire item unknown. Is that desired? If freight unknown, GMV with freight unknown. Probably yes, unknown amount not 0. Could alternatively SUM(price)+SUM(freight) with NULLs? But metric expression explicit SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value). Use exact.\n\nNeed valid order status filter in ON. The metric filter default attached. Since we want all members, ON condition. If I use subquery valid_orders and gmv separately maybe simpler. Need avoid duplicating all members if using multiple left joins with orders and order_items. It's okay due to COUNT DISTINCT and SUM per member. But SUM for member_gmv can be affected by multiple customers? already discussed. But also LEFT JOIN orders and order_items: for each valid order, multiple items sum. Correct. COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) counts valid orders per member. Good. If a member has multiple customer_unique_id? member has one. Good.\n\nCould there be members with same member_id but multiple level? no.\n\nNeed maybe use COUNT(*) vs COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id) in outer: member_orders has one row per member_id, level_id. If same member_id cannot have multiple level_id (members level_id single). COUNT(*) fine. If there are duplicate member_id? no primary. COUNT(*) equals members count per level. Good.\n\nNeed include ORDER BY level_id. Limit? Must LIMIT unless single row aggregate without group by. We have GROUP BY, so need LIMIT. How many levels? Unknown. Rule 3: 必须LIMIT. Default TopN? The question doesn't specify top; but must LIMIT. Could use LIMIT 1000? Hmm hard rule says must LIMIT. Need add LIMIT maybe 1000 to include all? But \"按会员等级ID统计\" no top N. We need output all levels, but rule says must LIMIT. Use LIMIT 100? There may be small number. Need choose. Usually in these tasks, for grouped results with no explicit N, use LIMIT 1000? We must comply. Could use LIMIT 1000 as safe. But may be considered arbitrary. They often expect LIMIT 100? We need include all likely <100. Use LIMIT 1000. Need not order? Order by level_id. That's okay.\n\nNeed output only SQL no code fence. Could include comment? Rule 18 allows comment for complex multi-table. But user requests direct SQL. We can include one-line comment? It says direct output executable SQL no explanation. Better no comment unless allowed. But \"复杂多表关联时，可在SELECT首行加一行--注释说明思路，紧接完整SQL。\" Optional. Simpler no comment.\n\nLet's verify if \"人均有效订单数\" denominator all members by level, yes. If membership status includes frozen/canceled, we include all. Good.\n\nNeed consider \"全部会员数（含无有效订单）\" maybe should count members with no valid orders but still have orders? Our all members. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If we start from members and left join customers, there might be duplicate member rows due to customers multiple same unique? Actually member -> customers via customer_unique_id. If a member's customer_unique_id has multiple customer_id rows, member row duplicates per customer. Then outer COUNT(*) would overcount members if not grouped by member first. We group member_orders by member_id, level_id, so duplicates collapse because we aggregate by member. Good. But member_gmv sums orders across all customer_id rows. valid_orders distinct. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If a member has multiple customer_unique_id? no.\n\nPotential issue: If same member has multiple members? no.\n\nNeed maybe use COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id) in outer instead of COUNT(*) to be safe. Since member_orders one row per member. Use COUNT(DISTINCT member_id) AS member_count. But group by level_id; if same member appears once. COUNT(*) fine. Use COUNT(*) as member_count. But if level_id null? Group by null; count includes. Level IDs maybe all nonnull. If null member level? \"按会员等级ID\" includes NULL? Maybe yes. We don't filter. ORDER BY level_id nulls last? default ASC nulls last in PostgreSQL? Actually ASC nulls last by default? PostgreSQL: nulls last for ASC? Default NULLS LAST for ASC? I think default is NULLS LAST for ASC, NULLS FIRST for DESC? Wait PostgreSQL default: ASC => NULLS LAST, DESC => NULLS FIRST. Actually maybe yes. We can specify NULLS LAST. Not necessary. But rule 8 says普通列表保留未知且NULLS LAST. Use ORDER BY level_id NULLS LAST.\n\nNeed maybe avoid using AVG(member_gmv) because member_gmv is numeric? price/freight numeric, SUM numeric, AVG numeric. ROUND numeric. Good.\n\nNeed人均有效订单数: SUM(valid_orders)::numeric / NULLIF(COUNT(*),0). valid_orders is bigint. Sum bigint. Cast to numeric. NULLIF count integer. division numeric. ROUND(...,2). Good.\n\nNeed aliases maybe Chinese? Could use english. The problem Chinese; output columns can be Chinese aliases? SQL identifiers with Chinese no quotes? In PostgreSQL unquoted Chinese? Actually identifiers can include Unicode letters? PostgreSQL allows letters with diacritics? It may allow Chinese? Unquoted? It might fold? To avoid issues, use English aliases. The user didn't require column names. Fine.\n\nPotential issue: \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" could mean average GMV per *member with known GMV* within level, not including zero. We do AVG(member_gmv) ignoring NULL. Good.\n\nLet's consider if the valid order filter for GMV should be applied. Metric gmv_with_freight has default filter o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable'). The question says \"已知含运费GMV\" likely uses that metric. Apply. It also says \"人均有效订单数\" valid_order. Both same filter. Good.\n\nBut if user explicitly says \"全部会员数（含无有效订单）\" and \"人均有效订单数\", maybe valid orders are only valid_order. Yes.\n\nNeed decide whether to use member_orders CTE or subquery. CTE okay. Must output one SELECT. WITH ... SELECT is one statement. Rule says only output one SELECT; CTE includes SELECT but final is SELECT. Usually allowed? It says 只输出一条SELECT；禁止... A WITH query is a SELECT statement. Should be acceptable. Could avoid CTE using subquery. But WITH is okay? To be safe, use subquery in FROM:\n\nSELECT level_id,\n       COUNT(*) AS member_count,\n       ROUND(SUM(valid_orders)::numeric / NULLIF(COUNT(*),0), 2) AS avg_valid_orders_per_member,\n       ROUND(AVG(member_gmv), 2) AS avg_member_gmv\nFROM (\n  SELECT m.member_id, m.level_id,\n         COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS valid_orders,\n         SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) AS member_gmv\n  FROM members m\n  LEFT JOIN customers c ON c.customer_unique_id = m.customer_unique_id\n  LEFT JOIN orders o ON o.customer_id = c.customer_id\n                    AND o.order_status NOT IN ('canceled','unavailable')\n  LEFT JOIN order_items oi ON oi.order_id = o.order_id\n  GROUP BY m.member_id, m.level_id\n) t\nGROUP BY level_id\nORDER BY level_id NULLS LAST\nLIMIT 1000;\n\nThis is one SELECT. Good.\n\nBut wait: In subquery, LEFT JOIN orders with ON status filter. Then LEFT JOIN order_items ON oi.order_id = o.order_id. For canceled orders, o.order_id is NULL, so oi won't join because oi.order_id = NULL false. Good. For valid orders, order_items join. member_gmv sums. valid_orders counts distinct o.order_id. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If a member has multiple customers with same unique, orders across multiple customer_ids. The subquery groups by member, so GMV sums all. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If a member has no customers, member_gmv NULL, valid_orders 0. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If a member has valid orders but order_items table missing for some orders, member_gmv sums existing items only. Is that \"known GMV\"? The metric SUM over order_items. If an order has no order_items, unknown? Actually no product amount fact maybe NULL. Our member_gmv could be non-null if some items, ignoring missing items. Is that acceptable? \"无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值\" means if no product amount fact for the member, NULL. If member has some order_items, we use known. Missing order items not represented, not zero. If order has no items, contributes nothing; if member has other items, member_gmv is sum of known items. Could be considered undercount but not specified. The metric uses order_items. Fine.\n\nNeed maybe count all members per level but member_orders groups by member_id, level_id. If a member has level_id null, included. Good.\n\nNeed verify \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" maybe it is average over orders, not members? The phrase \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" could mean per member level, average of GMV for members. The problem: \"按会员等级ID统计全部会员数（含无有效订单）、人均有效订单数；同时统计会员已知含运费GMV的平均值，无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值，不把未知金额当0。\" It explicitly says \"会员已知...GMV的平均值\" and \"无商品金额事实为NULL不参与GMV均值\". That indicates average per member across members, with NULL for no facts. Yes.\n\nCould also be average GMV per valid order? But \"会员已知含运费GMV的平均值\" likely average per member. The mention \"无商品金额事实\" per member. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"含无有效订单\" means count all members, and for avg valid orders denominator all members. We did. For GMV average, members with no valid orders have NULL and don't participate. They didn't say include them as 0. They explicitly say no product amount fact NULL not participate. Good.\n\nNeed maybe use COUNT(DISTINCT m.member_id) in outer rather than COUNT(*) because if same member_id appears multiple level_id? no. But if there are duplicate rows in members? primary. Good.\n\nNeed maybe round avg_valid_orders to 2. Yes.\n\nLet's think about whether to join member_levels. The question asks \"按会员等级ID\" not name. Members.level_id is enough. If there are level IDs in members not in member_levels, include. Good. If they wanted only existing levels? No.\n\nNeed not include level_name. Rule 8: 未要求名称，用当前事实/实体表已有标识，不补展示关联或名称. So only level_id.\n\nNeed maybe include status? No.\n\nNeed maybe use COUNT(*) AS member_count includes all members per level. If level_id null, group. Good.\n\nNeed maybe output columns order: level_id, member_count, avg_valid_orders_per_member, avg_member_gmv. That matches question.\n\nNeed ensure SQL executable with PostgreSQL. Aliases unquoted. NULLS LAST after ORDER BY level_id. LIMIT 1000. Good.\n\nLet's consider if SUM(oi.price + oi.freight_value) per member is affected by orders with multiple order_items: yes correct. But COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) per member counts valid orders. However if a member has multiple customer_unique_id? no.\n\nPotential issue: If a member's customer_unique_id matches multiple customers, and those customers have orders, then a single order belongs to one customer. no duplication. But what if the same order appears via multiple customer records? An order has one customer_id; only one customer row with that customer_id. So no.\n\nPotential issue: If a member has same member_id? no.\n\nNeed answer final with only SQL. No code fence. Let's provide. \nWait, rule says \"只输出一条SELECT；禁止...\" A WITH query is okay but our query has subquery. Final SQL starts SELECT. Good.\n\nLet's final."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3324,"completion_tokens":5007,"total_tokens":8331,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4790},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1532},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}